# What the image build never needs. The Dockerfile copies mix.exs, mix.lock, config/,
# apps/ and native/ and nothing else, so most of this is about the context Docker tars
# up before the first instruction runs — a checkout with `_build` and `deps` in it is a
# gigabyte of that — and about not letting a laptop's build outputs into a Linux image.
.git
_build
deps
node_modules
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
erl_crash.dump

# Built for the host, which is not the image's platform. The worker release builds its
# own inside the image, and a stale one from a laptop would be the wrong architecture
# with the right name.
apps/*/priv/reaper

# `mix release` compiles lib/ and nothing under test/. The fixtures are the tests'.
test
apps/*/test
fixtures

# Documentation and the chart are read by people and by CI, not by the release.
docs
charts
dev
scripts
*.md
